    "id": "pr-long-short",
    "title": "Long vs short vowels",
    "focus": "Vowel length",
    "tip": "Vowel length can change meaning. Long vowels (aa, ee, oo) are held noticeably longer than short ones (a, i, u). English speakers often shorten them — exaggerate at first.",
