  {
    "id": "pr-aspiration",
    "title": "Breathy consonants",
    "focus": "Plain vs aspirated: p/ph, k/kh, b/bh, ch/chh, g/gh",
    "tip": "Hold your hand in front of your mouth. Aspirated sounds (written with h: ph, kh, bh, chh, gh) release a clear puff of air; plain ones release almost none. \"Ph\" is NOT \"f\" in careful speech — it's p + breath.",
