  {
    "id": "pr-nasal",
    "title": "Nasal vowels",
    "focus": "Final -n in main, hain, nahin",
    "tip": "In words like main, hain and nahin, the n is usually not a full n. Instead, the vowel goes through your nose. Try saying the vowel while letting air out through your nose, without touching your tongue to the roof of your mouth.",
